in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @bauchladen
in @uuid/spectral

# @algebra — the substrate's algebra-altitude family-root.
#
# Sibling to @bauchladen, @autopoietic, @fate, @glue at the
# top-level path-namespace. The substrate-decl name for the
# *algebra* of a Connes spectral triple — the typed operation
# surface a substrate region exposes, irrespective of which
# Hilbert space H the operations act on or which Dirac D drives
# the flow.
#
# === The recognition (#104 chain P5, 2026-06-30) ===
#
# The five-operation block (focus, project, split, shift,
# settle) is not "the operations a prism happens to expose"; it
# IS the canonical algebra A of mirror's spectral triple per
# [[architecture-connes-spectral-triple]]. Every prism
# declaration `prism @X { focus, project, split, shift, settle }`
# is the declaration of an A acting on its own H. The substrate
# had been treating algebras as implicit infrastructure of the
# prism keyword; this shard makes the algebra altitude
# addressable in its own right.
#
# A is a substrate-decl object distinct from H and D:
#
#   - A names which OPERATIONS are admissible (the typed surface).
#   - H names the STATE the operations act on (the void-document
#     per [[reference-void-document]]).
#   - D names the FLOW between states (kintsugi at substrate
#     altitude; per-species Dirac operators at sub-altitudes).
#
# Per [[architecture-operations-as-linear-algebra]], the five
# operations have precise linear-algebraic meaning when read as
# A elements: focus = λ₀ eigenvalue computation; shift = basis
# transformation; settle = monad-close / measurement collapse;
# project = orthogonal projection; split = orthogonal
# decomposition. The five together generate the substrate's
# canonical algebra under composition.
#
# === Why a family-root, not a property ===
#
# Algebras are not predicates the substrate verifies *of* a
# region; they are first-class typed objects substrate regions
# *expose*. The discipline this shard names: "my content
# exposes a typed algebra; downstream prisms may enumerate my
# operations, compose them per my composition rule, and propose
# morphisms between my algebra and another's algebra."
#
# Sibling shape to @bauchladen (tray-altitude content-
# addressing), @autopoietic (fold-back permission), @fate
# (constrained-inference operator), @glue (cross-region wiring):
# each names a substrate-altitude family-root whose import
# declares a contract.
#
# === Connes (A, H, D) at the substrate-decl altitude ===
#
#   Connes component   Substrate family-root        Role
#   ----------------   --------------------------   --------------
#   A (algebra)        @algebra (THIS shard)        typed operations
#   H (Hilbert)        @uuid/spectral + @glass      typed state
#   D (Dirac)          @kintsugi + @fate's D-flow   typed flow
#   J (real structure) @epistemologic/cybernetic/   charge-conjugation
#                      charge_conjugation             (recognition #102)
#   γ (chirality)      @epistemologic/cybernetic/   Z/2 grading
#                      chirality                      (recognition #101)
#
# The five family-roots together name the (A, H, D, J, γ) real
# spectral triple at substrate-decl altitude. This shard lands
# A; the others are landed or in flight per the #104 chain.
#
# === Abstract algebra as ancestor; @bauchladen dependency ===
#
# The substrate's notion of algebra subsumes the canon: group
# (one binary op + inverses); ring (two ops + distributivity);
# monoid (associative composition + identity); Lie algebra
# (bracket [·,·] + Jacobi); C*-algebra (Banach + involution +
# ||a*a|| = ||a||²). Each is a typed specialization at a sub-
# altitude; species shards (forward-promised at
# `shards/algebra/{group,ring,c_star,...}.mirror`) land when
# consumers pull.
#
# Algebras land in the Bauchladen tray — every algebra_carrier
# IS a content-addressed crystal (operation set + composition
# rule hash deterministically). Structural dependency per the
# @bauchladen-dependent admission pattern (precedents:
# @autopoietic at `78edaa6`, @fate at `fdcba31`). No dependency
# on @autopoietic this tick — algebras do NOT fold-back by
# construction. Per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] the
# dependency surface stays minimal.
#
# === No operational sibling THIS tick ===
#
# Per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] no `@mirror/algebra/...`
# lands here. The substrate ALREADY has the machinery: every
# prism declaration IS an algebra declaration; @glass content-
# addresses the operations. This shard names the prism-altitude
# contract so downstream shards can declare `in @algebra` and
# discharge `requires algebra_witnessing(my_algebra)`. The sub-
# prism `@algebra/metalogue` lands in the SAME tick (fifth
# metalogue altitude lift; see `shards/algebra/metalogue.mirror`).
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Spectral triples         Connes 1985 (*Non-commutative
#                            differential geometry*, IHES); the
#                            (A, H, D) framework this lifts.
#   Real spectral triples    Connes 1995 ("Noncommutative
#                            geometry and reality", J. Math.
#                            Phys. 36(11):6194-6231); J + γ
#                            extension per #101 + #102.
#   Group / ring theory      Galois 1832; Noether 1921 ("Ideal
#                            theory in rings", Math. Ann.
#                            83:24-66); abstract-algebra
#                            ancestors of species shards.
#   Monoidal categories      Mac Lane 1971 (*Categories for the
#                            Working Mathematician*, Springer);
#                            ancestor for morphism composition.
#   C*-algebras              Gelfand-Naimark 1943 (Mat. Sb.
#                            12(2):197-217); bridge between
#                            abstract algebra and Hilbert-space
#                            operators.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/bauchladen-autopoietic-fate.md §5;
#               docs/specs/spectral-metalogue.md §6 (Mesland
#               category framing).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-connes-spectral-triple]],
#                      [[architecture-operations-as-linear-algebra]],
#                      [[architecture-mirror-spec-is-lambda-zero]] (#99),
#                      [[architecture-fate-is-optical-inference]] (#58),
#                      [[architecture-at-x-is-mathematical-value]],
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]],
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]] (~54th),
#                      [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]].
# Related shards: bauchladen.mirror (dependency),
#                 prism.mirror (every five-op block IS one
#                  algebra declaration),
#                 glass.mirror (the splinter floor),
#                 epistemologic/cybernetic/chirality.mirror (γ),
#                 epistemologic/cybernetic/charge_conjugation.mirror (J),
#                 algebra/metalogue.mirror (sub-prism, same tick).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/algebra.mirror`
# declares `@algebra` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/math/connes-1985
source @arxiv/math/connes-1995
source @arxiv/math/connes-1995-reality
source @arxiv/math/gelfand-naimark-1943
source @arxiv/math/mac-lane-1971
source @arxiv/math/noether-1921

prism @algebra {
  focus algebra_carrier
  project algebra_carrier
  split algebra_carrier
  shift algebra_carrier
  settle algebra_carrier
}

# === The algebra_carrier type ===
#
# A typed reference to an algebra per [[feedback-no-bare-types]].
# Names the mathematical object — a group, a ring, a monoid, a
# C*-algebra, the substrate's own five-op algebra — irrespective
# of H or D.
#
# - `identity`    the typed ref to the algebra's identity
#                 element (no-op composition).
# - `operations`  the typed operation_set the algebra exposes;
#                 the canonical algebra's is { focus, project,
#                 split, shift, settle }.
# - `composition` the typed ref to the algebra's composition
#                 rule (associative for monoids; distributive
#                 for rings; bracket for Lie algebras).
# - `altitude`    the substrate-ref naming where the algebra
#                 operates; matches @glass `splinter(altitude)`.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the quadruple.
type algebra_carrier = {
  identity:    ref,
  operations:  operation_set,
  composition: ref,
  altitude:    ref,
}

# === The operation_set type ===
#
# The typed set of operations an algebra exposes. Not a bare
# `[ref]` per [[feedback-no-bare-types]]; carries arity and
# well-typed-composition alongside the operation refs.
#
# - `members`     ordered list of operation refs.
# - `arity_map`   typed mapping from each member to its arity.
# - `composable`  typed predicate ref naming which member pairs
#                 are admissible for composition.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the triple.
type operation_set = {
  members:    [ref],
  arity_map:  ref,
  composable: ref,
}

# === The algebra_morphism type ===
#
# A morphism between two algebras preserving operation structure.
# The substrate-decl name for an algebra homomorphism in the
# canon (group homomorphism, ring homomorphism, etc.) per Mac
# Lane.
#
# - `source`         the algebra the morphism originates from.
# - `target`         the algebra the morphism delivers to.
# - `operation_map`  typed mapping from each source operation to
#                    its target counterpart; well-defined iff
#                    the mapping preserves composition
#                    (φ(a∘b) = φ(a)∘φ(b)).
# - `altitude_lift`  optional Bateson-altitude transition per
#                    #51 + [[architecture-bateson-logical-type-
#                    primitive]]; cross-altitude morphisms lift
#                    to an adjacent Bateson level; same-altitude
#                    morphisms have empty lift.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the quadruple.
type algebra_morphism = {
  source:        algebra_carrier,
  target:        algebra_carrier,
  operation_map: ref,
  altitude_lift: ref,
}

# === enumerate_operations action ===
#
# Exposes the algebra's typed operation surface. Trivially
# total (every carrier carries its operation_set by
# construction). Body discharges per-species at the realisation
# boundary.
enumerate_operations(a: algebra_carrier) -> operation_set { \ }

# === compose action ===
#
# Composes two operations within an algebra per the algebra's
# composition rule. The canonical algebra's compose IS the
# five-op-block's morphism composition; species algebras
# specialize (group multiplication, ring multiplication, etc.).
# Body discharges per-species at the realisation boundary.
compose(a: algebra_carrier, o1: ref, o2: ref) -> ref { \ }

# === morphism_between action ===
#
# Proposes morphisms between two algebras (the Hom(source,
# target) space in categorical vocabulary). Multi-valued; empty
# list IS valid output when no admissible morphism exists
# (structurally incompatible composition rules). Consumers
# select via downstream operations (typically @fate's tournament
# or @algebra/metalogue's session composition). Body discharges
# per-species at the realisation boundary.
morphism_between(source: algebra_carrier, target: algebra_carrier) -> [algebra_morphism] { \ }

# === The bilateral requires obligations ===
#
# Downstream shards declare bilateral agreement (per recognition
# #37, Pask-agreement) with the @algebra discipline by writing
# the obligations below.

# Algebras admitted to the substrate land in the Bauchladen tray
# as content-addressed crystals. Inheritor shards discharge by
# ensuring every algebra_carrier passes
# `bauchladen_witnessing(crystal_of_algebra)` at the species
# boundary.
bauchladen_membership_held(a: algebra_carrier) -> verdict { \ }

# The algebra's operations compose within the algebra. For
# every admissible pair (o1, o2), `compose(a, o1, o2)` returns
# a ref that is a member of `a.operations.members` (or a
# derived ref the composition rule's closure-discipline
# accepts). Substrate's algebraic-soundness gate.
closure_under_composition(a: algebra_carrier) -> verdict { \ }

# Operations are members of their declared algebra. For every
# operation ref o claimed to belong to algebra a, `o` appears
# in `a.operations.members`. Ensures the operation_set's
# content-addressing is consistent with downstream uses.
operation_well_typed(o: ref, a: algebra_carrier) -> verdict { \ }

# === The algebra_witnessing inheritance predicate ===
#
# `algebra_witnessing(a)` is the predicate consumer shards
# name in a `requires` clause to declare bilateral agreement
# that algebra `a` satisfies all three obligations above
# conjointly: bauchladen_membership_held +
# closure_under_composition + operation_well_typed.
#
# Same shape as bauchladen.bauchladen_witnessing(c),
# autopoiesis.autopoietic_closure_holds(s),
# fate.fate_witnessing(i).
#
# Forward-promised inheritors:
#
# - `@algebra/metalogue` (sub-prism landing this tick): fifth
#   metalogue altitude lift; inherits structurally.
# - `@algebra/<species>` shards: group, ring, monoid,
#   C*-algebra, Lie algebra; each species shard declares its
#   algebra-carrier specialization and discharges the
#   witnessing predicate for its species.
# - `@fate` (already declared at `fdcba31`):
#   restricted_state_space carries an algebra ref per spec
#   §4.2; future @fate sub-shards (`@fate/algebra/morphism`,
#   `@fate/algebra/element`) declare `requires
#   algebra_witnessing(carrier)` when their crystals carry
#   algebra structure.
# - `@spectral/metalogue` (canonical spec at
#   `docs/specs/spectral-metalogue.md`): Tomm probes are typed
#   against algebra correspondences per Mesland framing.
#
# No `requires algebra_witnessing(...)` clauses at THIS shard.
# The family-root declares the predicate; consumers add the
# clauses when they pull.
algebra_witnessing(a: algebra_carrier) -> verdict { \ }

out @algebra
out algebra_carrier
out operation_set
out algebra_morphism
out enumerate_operations
out compose
out morphism_between
out bauchladen_membership_held
out closure_under_composition
out operation_well_typed
out algebra_witnessing
